{{!--
    Stations tab (#8, #24): the five fixed crew roles (CONTEXT.md's "Station" entry), each a card
    holding its enable/disable toggle, its crew assignments and its Station actions.

    Layout is #21's prototype variant B: a Station is a card whose header carries the title, the
    crew collapsed into an overlapping avatar strip and the enable toggle, with the Station's
    actions below. The actions are the tab's primary affordance - the crew list shrank into the
    header to make room for them.

    The actions render as the character sheet's own Features tab renders features: one
    `dhscifi.inventory-item` row per feature inside an `.items-list` (daggerheart's
    `character/features.hbs` -> `daggerheart.inventory-item`), so a Station action gets the same
    portrait / name / tags / click-to-expand description / action buttons below. The Roller label
    rides along as the row's first tag. `pressAction="useStationAction"` swaps the row's `useItem`
    for this sheet's own press handler on both the portrait and the action buttons.

    `fieldset.glassy` is kept as the card, but *without* a `legend`: daggerheart themes a glassy
    fieldset's legend as a small padded pill sitting on the border line (`.dh-style fieldset.glassy
    legend`), which is the wrong container for a 28px avatar strip. The card background comes for
    free from the unscoped `fieldset.glassy` rule (docs/adr/0002's "copied by value" addenda); the
    header row is ours and is styled in `main.scss`. `.drop-section` comes along
    for structural parity with the system's own markup but is inert here (it is scoped to
    `.class .tab.settings` upstream), same as it was before this tab became cards. `.actors-dragger`
    (the dashed "drop actors here" hint) is the party sheet's own class and *is* `.party`-scoped
    there, so its rule is copied by value into `main.scss`.

    A crew avatar is NOT a `dhscifi.inventory-item` row and not even the row skeleton it used to
    borrow: collapsed to a portrait, it carries only the two affordances it had - the portrait
    opens the Actor's sheet, and a hover-revealed "x" removes the assignment (editable only, since
    it mutates the ship). The name lives in the tooltip.

    A disabled station keeps rendering whatever crew it already has (disabling is non-destructive -
    see `SpaceshipData`'s `stationField`), just dimmed and without the drop hint; the drop handler
    refuses new assignments to it. Its Station actions render *no* rows at all (#24) while their
    items stay on the ship, so re-enabling restores them - `#buildStationsContext` empties the list
    rather than the template hiding it, so a disabled Station puts no pressable uuid in the DOM.

    Pressing a row's portrait or one of its action buttons goes through the sheet's `useStationAction` action (#25), which resolves the
    item's Roller before anything runs (`station-actions/press.ts`): a `ship` action is handed
    straight to the item's own `use(event)` - so a single-action feature rolls immediately and a
    multi-action one opens daggerheart's own `ActionSelectionDialog`, with the ship's traits and
    the ship's Hope/Stress, docs/adr/0003's `ship` branch; an action button skips the selection and
    runs its own action - while a `crew`/`ask` one first asks who
    acts and then runs the chosen action against that character. The station's `data-station` on
    the fieldset is what tells the handler whose crew to offer.
    Pressing is deliberately not gated on `@root.editable`: every Station's actions are pressable by
    anyone with access to the ship (#24), and a crewing player has exactly that as of #22. The
    row's mutating controls (kebab menu) still are, inside the partial.

    `stations` is built by `SpaceshipActorSheet.#buildStationsContext`, which is also where a UUID
    that no longer resolves becomes a `missing` entry rendered as "Unknown" instead of erroring.
--}}
<section class="tab {{tab.id}} {{tab.cssClass}} spaceship-stations" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}">
    <div class="stations-sections">
        {{#each stations as |station|}}
            <fieldset class="glassy drop-section station station-card{{#unless station.enabled}} station-disabled{{/unless}}"
                      data-station="{{station.id}}">
                {{!-- No `data-station` on the toggle, the avatars or the action rows: every station
                      control sits inside its own fieldset, and the sheet's `#getStationId` climbs
                      to the nearest `[data-station]`, so the fieldset's own attribute already
                      identifies the station for clicks and drops alike. --}}
                <div class="station-card-head">
                    <span class="station-title">{{localize station.label}}</span>

                    <div class="crew-strip">
                        {{#each station.crew as |assignment|}}
                            <div class="crew-avatar{{#if assignment.missing}} crew-avatar-missing{{/if}}"
                                 data-uuid="{{assignment.uuid}}">
                                {{!-- A resolved Actor's portrait opens its sheet, mirroring the
                                      party sheet's own `openDocument` affordance; a missing one
                                      has nothing to open, so it's inert. The name lives in the
                                      tooltip now that the strip has no room for a label, so the
                                      resolved portrait's tooltip carries both it and the
                                      "opens the sheet" hint the old row put on the portrait. --}}
                                <img src="{{assignment.img}}" alt="{{assignment.name}}"
                                     {{#if assignment.missing}}data-tooltip="{{assignment.name}}"
                                     {{else}}data-action="openCrew"
                                     data-tooltip="{{assignment.name}} - {{localize 'DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.OpenActor'}}"{{/if}} />

                                {{!-- Removing an assignment mutates the ship, so it follows
                                      `@root.editable` like every other mutating control on this
                                      sheet. `.delete-icon` is the party sheet's own class for the
                                      same affordance. --}}
                                {{#if @root.editable}}
                                    <a class="delete-icon" data-action="removeCrew"
                                       data-tooltip="{{localize 'DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.RemoveCrew.title'}}">
                                        <i class="fa-regular fa-fw fa-times" inert></i>
                                    </a>
                                {{/if}}
                            </div>
                        {{else}}
                            {{!-- An enabled Station with no crew already says so, larger, through
                                  the `.actors-dragger` hint below; a disabled one renders no hint
                                  (it refuses drops), so it gets the header line instead. --}}
                            {{#unless station.enabled}}
                                <span class="crew-empty">{{localize "DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.NoCrew"}}</span>
                            {{/unless}}
                        {{/each}}
                    </div>

                    {{#if @root.editable}}
                        <a class="station-toggle" data-action="toggleStation"
                           data-tooltip="{{#if station.enabled}}{{localize 'DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.Disable'}}{{else}}{{localize 'DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.Enable'}}{{/if}}">
                            <i class="fa-solid {{#if station.enabled}}fa-toggle-on{{else}}fa-toggle-off{{/if}}"></i>
                        </a>
                    {{/if}}
                </div>

                {{#if station.actions.length}}
                    <ul class="items-list station-actions">
                        {{#each station.actions as |entry|}}
                            {{> "dhscifi.inventory-item"
                                item=entry.item
                                tags=entry.tags
                                hasDescription=entry.hasDescription
                                usable=entry.usable
                                canChat=entry.canChat
                                pressAction="useStationAction"
                            }}
                        {{/each}}
                    </ul>
                {{/if}}

                {{#if station.enabled}}
                    {{#unless station.crew.length}}
                        <div class="actors-dragger">
                            <span>{{localize "DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Stations.DropHere"}}</span>
                        </div>
                    {{/unless}}
                {{/if}}
            </fieldset>
        {{/each}}
    </div>
</section>
